      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The community began as a weekend getaway but now hosts nearly 850 homes and over 4,000 lots across 2,400 acres.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://lakewaynoka.com/about-us",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1974 the developer filed for bankruptcy, forcing residents to work unpaid at the gate while the lake stayed 95% complete.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        27,
        26
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://lakewaynoka.com/about-us",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The first WPOA Board of Trustees was elected after the lake reopened in 1976, marking the start of resident governance.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        29,
        30
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://lakewaynoka.com/about-us",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Lake Waynoka sits between Sardinia and Russellville in Brown County, Ohio, and is surrounded by a reservoir of the same name.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
